{"id":"small-donation-blocks","title":"Blocks of contributions in publicly financed campaigns","question":"In campaigns that received public matching funds, how many contributions arrived in same-day blocks from people naming one employer, and how concentrated were contributions on a single day?","finding":"90 publicly financed campaigns since 2014 reported 75,925 itemized contributions of $500 or less from individuals, 35,960 of them $150 or less. 45 same-day, same-employer blocks of five or more donors were found in 22 campaigns, covering 334 contributions (0.4% of the total); the highest share in one campaign is 6% (JEFF SHEEHY FOR SUPERVISOR JUNE 2018, 2018). Donors are counted and not named.","how":"Committees are those shown receiving public funds in the public-financing screen. For each, itemized contributions from individuals of $500 or less are grouped by date and by the employer the donor stated (blank, retired, self-employed and public employers left out); a block is five or more different donors with one employer on one day. 'Small blocks' are blocks made only of gifts of $150 or less. The top day is the single date with most contributions. Share from outside the city uses the donor's postal code. The same-employer test at the maximum gift, for all candidates, is in the “late screens” results and is not repeated.","limits":"A block is what a workplace fundraiser, a union endorsement or a house party hosted by colleagues looks like, and campaigns record contributions in batches on the day they are deposited, which alone puts unrelated donors on one date. The filings give no street address, so contributions from one address cannot be tested. Which contributions were submitted for matching, and which the Ethics Commission refused, is in its audit files, not in these statements; the matchable amount changed over the years (the Budget and Legislative Analyst's 2019 report gives $100 for the first tier then), so $150 is a round cut-off, not the legal one. Employer names are typed by donors and vary in spelling, which hides some blocks.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"committee","t":"Candidate committee","type":"text"},{"k":"year","t":"Election","type":"year"},{"k":"contributions","t":"Contributions of $500 or less from individuals","type":"int"},{"k":"small","t":"Of which $150 or less","type":"int"},{"k":"smallShare","t":"Share $150 or less","type":"pct"},{"k":"topDay","t":"Busiest day","type":"date"},{"k":"topDayN","t":"Contributions that day","type":"int"},{"k":"topDayShare","t":"Share on that day","type":"pct"},{"k":"blocks","t":"Same-day, same-employer blocks of 5 or more","type":"int"},{"k":"blockDonors","t":"Contributions in blocks","type":"int"},{"k":"blockShare","t":"Share in blocks","type":"pct"},{"k":"smallBlocks","t":"Blocks of gifts of $150 or less","type":"int"},{"k":"largest","t":"Largest block","type":"int"},{"k":"largestEmployer","t":"Employer named in the largest block","type":"text"},{"k":"largestDay","t":"Its date","type":"date"},{"k":"outside","t":"Share from outside San Francisco postal codes","type":"pct"}],"rows":[{"committee":"JEFF SHEEHY FOR SUPERVISOR JUNE 2018","year":2018,"contributions":474,"small":91,"smallShare":0.192,"topDay":"2017-10-18","topDayN":61,"topDayShare":0.129,"blocks":3,"blockDonors":29,"blockShare":0.061,"smallBlocks":null,"largest":13,"largestEmployer":"Build Group","largestDay":"2017-10-18","outside":0.27},{"committee":"Aaron Peskin for Supervisor 2020","year":2020,"contributions":624,"small":223,"smallShare":0.357,"topDay":"2019-06-25","topDayN":35,"topDayShare":0.056,"blocks":2,"blockDonors":18,"blockShare":0.029,"smallBlocks":null,"largest":9,"largestEmployer":"Able Services","largestDay":"2020-03-12","outside":0.263},{"committee":"Jessica Ho for Supervisor 2018","year":2018,"contributions":437,"small":176,"smallShare":0.403,"topDay":"2018-06-29","topDayN":26,"topDayShare":0.059,"blocks":1,"blockDonors":11,"blockShare":0.025,"smallBlocks":null,"largest":11,"largestEmpl